      "name": "Base of village cross, opposite the Grange",
      "designationType": "listed_building",
      "sourceUrl": "https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1130185?section=official-list-entry",
      "officialName": "Base of village cross, opposite the Grange",
      "details": "This list entry was subject to a Minor Amendment on 14/04/2020\n\nTL 27 SW\n\n8/83\n\nBRAMPTON\n\nHIGH STREET (North Side)\n\nBase of village cross, opposite the Grange\n\nGV \n\nII\n\nProbably C14 limestone base of village cross, resited. Square with chamfered and stopped corners, on C20 plinth.\n\nListing NGR: TL2081071073"
    },
    {
      "featureId": "historic-england:nhle:1317518",
      "listEntry": "1317518",
      "name": "GLEN COTTAGE",
      "designationType": "listed_building",
      "sourceUrl": "https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1317518?section=official-list-entry",
      "officialName": "Glen Cottage",
      "details": "TL 27 SW BRAMPTON GROVE LANE (East Side)\n\n13/63 No. 10 - (Glen Cottage)\n\nGV II\n\nEarly C18 cottage of two unit plan. Timber framed, rendered with thatched roof and red brick ridge stack. Small recessed panel with date 17(3?) and initials V.S. beneath. One storey and attic. Two C20 casements. Later entry in extension to north gable end.\n\nListing NGR: TL2090471137"
    }
  ],
